# open-kali-claude configuration.
#
# Copy to ".env" (it is git-ignored) and edit. Everything here is optional —
# the defaults shown are what the container uses out of the box.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# NOTE on precedence: for the knobs the script itself needs (port, model,
# image/container/volume names, bind host), a value exported in your shell wins
# over this file, which wins over the built-in default. The whole file is also
# passed into the container (docker --env-file), so any opencode/provider env
# var you add below is visible to opencode inside the container.

# ---- Model / provider (opencode uses "provider/model") ----------------------
# OPENCODE_PROVIDER + OPENCODE_MODEL are combined into "provider/model".
# If OPENCODE_MODEL already contains a "/", it is used as-is.
# List what your login can actually use with:  ./okc.sh connect  ->  opencode models anthropic
OPENCODE_PROVIDER=anthropic
OPENCODE_MODEL=claude-sonnet-4-5
# Examples of other valid values:
#   OPENCODE_MODEL=claude-opus-4-5
#   OPENCODE_MODEL=claude-sonnet-4-5          # combined with provider above
#   OPENCODE_MODEL=anthropic/claude-opus-4-5  # fully-qualified, ignores OPENCODE_PROVIDER
# Optional lighter model for cheap tasks (title generation, etc.):
# OPENCODE_SMALL_MODEL=claude-haiku-4-5

# ---- Authentication ----------------------------------------------------------
# Preferred: sign in interactively with OAuth (Claude Pro/Max) — it is stored in
# the persisted volume and survives restarts:
#     ./okc.sh connect   ->   opencode auth login
#
# Alternative: use an API key instead of OAuth. If set in your shell or here it
# is forwarded to the container and opencode picks it up automatically.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# ---- Networking --------------------------------------------------------------
# Host port and the interface it binds to. The default binds to localhost only,
# because the opencode API can run arbitrary commands/tools. Only expose it on a
# routable address if you ALSO set a server password below and understand the risk.
OPENCODE_PORT=4096
OKC_BIND_HOST=127.0.0.1

# Optional HTTP basic auth for the opencode server (username defaults to "opencode").
# OPENCODE_SERVER_PASSWORD=change-me
# OPENCODE_SERVER_USERNAME=opencode

# ---- Infra / naming (rarely needed) -----------------------------------------
# OKC_IMAGE=open-kali-claude:latest
# OKC_CONTAINER=open-kali-claude
# OKC_VOLUME=open-kali-claude-auth
# OKC_SHELL=/bin/bash
# Bind-mount a host project into /work so the agent's file changes are visible
# on the host (grants the agent access to those files):
# OKC_WORKDIR=/absolute/path/to/your/project

# ---- Build-time knobs (used by './okc.sh build' / first './okc.sh run') ------
# Kali toolset: kali-linux-headless (default) | kali-linux-core | none
# KALI_METAPACKAGE=kali-linux-headless
# NODE_MAJOR=22
# OPENCODE_VERSION=latest
# CLAUDE_CODE_VERSION=latest
